---
description: Database access must be in service files, not page files
alwaysApply: true
---

# Backend Code Goes in Services

NEVER write Prisma/database access code directly in `+page.server.ts` or `+server.ts` files.

ALL database operations MUST go in service files under `src/lib/server/services/`.

## Correct Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ src/lib/server/services/teams.ts
export async function getTeamById(id: number) {
  return await prisma.team.findUnique({ where: { id } });
}

// ✅ src/routes/teams/[id]/+page.server.ts
import { getTeamById } from '$lib/server/services/teams';

export const load = async ({ params }) => {
  const team = await getTeamById(parseInt(params.id));
  return { team };
};
```

## Wrong Pattern

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - src/routes/teams/[id]/+page.server.ts
import { prisma } from '$lib/server/db';

export const load = async ({ params }) => {
  // BAD: Direct prisma access in page file
  const team = await prisma.team.findUnique({ where: { id: parseInt(params.id) } });
  return { team };
};
```

## Service File Location

`src/lib/server/services/<domain>.ts`

Examples: `teams.ts`, `matches.ts`, `notifications.ts`, `users.ts`
